                "@id": "https://w3c.github.io/rdf-tests/rdf/rdf11/rdf-mt/manifest.ttl#rdfs-subClassOf-a-Property-test001",
                "@type": [
                  "mf:NegativeEntailmentTest",
                  "TestCriterion",
                  "TestCase"
                ],
                "title": "rdfs-subClassOf-a-Property-test001",
                "rdfs:comment": "\n    an instance of the Property class may have an rdfs:subClassOf\n    property. the meaning of such a property is defined by the\n    model theory. The wording of the formal resolution is a bit\n    bare, so let me add a few words of explanation. What this\n    means is that a resource can be both a class and a property.\n    This test is encoded as follows: a Property may have a\n    subclass (that is, such an RDF graph is satisfiable)\n  ",
                "http://www.w3.org/ns/rdftest#approval": {
                  "@id": "http://www.w3.org/ns/rdftest#Approved"
                },
                "mf:entailmentRegime": "RDFS",
